  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n7-6x-{x}^{2}>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny=7-6x-{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/8e12975187d46b6dc408e21234309e33654a24503db65ed075e32990de8ed654.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-7<x<1.$",
